The flat is small.
But there is furniture.
There stands a sofa by the wall.
I drop my bag on the sofa.
Then I walk past the table and over to the window.
I pull back the curtains.
The light fills the whole room.
But it is very cold here!
The radiator sits under the window.
I touch it.
It is completely cold.
I turn the knob.
Nothing happens.
It is still cold.
"The heat doesn't work," I say.
I am freezing.
I must find the caretaker.
